# 4. Dynamic Department Routes
Do **not** create pages such as:
```text
/hrmo
/mpdc
/assessor
/rhu
```
as separate hardcoded implementations.
Use one dynamic route.
Preferred public route:
```text
/departments/[slug]
```
Examples:
```text
/departments/hrmo
/departments/mpdc
/departments/assessor
/departments/rhu
/departments/engineering
```
All pages must use the same reusable Department page structure.
The page must load the Department from the database using the slug.
Example logic:
```text
slug = "hrmo"
Find Department where:
department.slug === "hrmo"
```
If the department does not exist or is inactive, handle it properly with the existing application's 404/not-found behavior.
