# Final Requirement
The final architecture should essentially behave like this:
```text
Department
│
├── Department Head
├── News[]
├── Programs[]
├── Contacts[]
│
└── Users[]
```
And:
```text
User
│
├── Role
│   ├── SUPERADMIN
│   ├── EDITOR
│   └── LEGISLATIVE_EDITOR if still necessary
│
└── Department / Office Access
```
The important separation is:
```text
ROLE = what the user is allowed to do
DEPARTMENT = which office's data the user is allowed to manage
```
A new Department added through Superadmin must immediately become a first-class Department throughout the website without requiring another source-code modification.
Before finishing, review the implementation for any remaining hardcoded Department names, routes, office lists, role values, sidebar entries, or Department-specific conditional logic and replace them with dynamic database-driven behavior where appropriate.